  "body": "Found while fixing #600 (PR #607).\n\n**Today:** `vertex_pick.rs` decides whether a vertex is visible by testing the segment from the vertex to the camera's eye point. In Orthographic mode the view rays are parallel, so a vertex hidden behind geometry along the view direction can read as visible, and a visible one as hidden.\n\n**Expected:** in ortho, the visibility ray runs from the vertex back along −view-direction (parallel), as `ray_through` does for picks.\n\n**Done means:** a test with an occluded corner in ortho is not offered as pickable, a visible one is, and perspective is unchanged.",
